VSAA (Very Simple Random Access Archive)

Implemented in roughly 450 lines of Python code,
VSAA is a lightweight archive container format designed to be simple and auditable while supporting modern archive features:
- Streaming reads
- Efficient random file access
- Container-only mode(no compression)
- High compression ratio for simplicity
- Path safety
- CRC32 corruption detection
- Minimal integration friction
- Cross-platform interoperability

No external dependencies, just download and use.

For reimplementers: the SPEC file contains the complete VSAA format specification.